WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.201
EVAN RACHEL WOOD:
<i> It's always really hard for me</i>

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.936
<i> to look at photos of myself
 from before.</i>

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.972
♪ (MELLOW MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:09.275
I've kept this journal
since I was fifteen.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.246
"I made a new friend."
(MIMICS EXPLOSION)

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.148
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.951
<i> I'm here today
 to talk about Brian Warner,</i>

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.087 line:0%
also known to the world
as Marilyn Manson.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.356
♪ (UPLIFTING PIANO
MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.058
SARA LYNN MOORE:<i> He studied
 how to manipulate people.</i>

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.793
<i> He groomed her.</i>

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:28.894 line:0%
He's a predator.

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:30.430 line:0%
Everyone was looking
at Marilyn Manson,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.498
<i> and they weren't looking
 at Brian Warner.</i>

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.101
WOOD:<i> Numerous women
 heard my story,</i>

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.869
<i> and they knew
 exactly who it was.</i>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.672
I realized
that I wasn't the only one
that this had happened to.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.440
You're not alone.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.042
I know. It's crazy.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.811
WOOD:<i> We were outside of
 the statute of limitations,</i>

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:47.013
<i> we had run out of time,</i>

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.415
<i> and nothing in our evidence
 could help us.</i>

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:53.219
SPEAKER:
<i>Statistically, a lot of victims
 take seven to ten years</i>

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.088
<i> to even recognize that they
 were a victim of this abuse.</i>

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.257
♪ (MUSIC SWELLS) ♪

00:00:58.357 --> 00:00:59.558
WOOD:<i> I became an activist,</i>

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:02.161 line:0%
<i> fighting for victims
 and survivors</i>

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.831
<i> of domestic violence
 and sexual assault.</i>

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:10.203
<i> Not only did people hear
 our stories, but they said,</i>

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.371
"Yeah, we hear you, and
something does need to change."

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:15.674
We need those that will expand
the statute of limitations.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.178
<i> It's really important
 to survivors like us.</i>

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.849
WOOD:<i> We need to make sure
 that this doesn't happen
 to anybody else.</i>

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.484
<i> I realized that
 this is the first time</i>

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:29.455
<i> I haven't been doubted
 or questioned or shamed.</i>

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:32.825
<i> This was the first time that
 someone was really listening.</i>

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:34.494
<i> I was like,
 "What is this feeling?"</i>

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.597
And it's this feeling
of being believed.

